# SOC with AI — Allowed SSH signers for commit verification
# Format: email key-type public-key
#
# To add a new signer:
#   1. Ask them for: ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "email@example.com" -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
#   2. Add their public key line below
#   3. Commit this file
#
# Verify a signed commit:
#   git log --show-signature -1 <commit>
#
# Bulk-verify recent commits:
#   git log --show-signature --oneline -20

# Example (replace with real keys):
# developer@example.com ssh-ed25519 AAAA...base64...key
